  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — namely, the skewness of the lotteries — is not considered by the individual. The individual focuses on expected value (which is equal in both cases) and on subjective utility or life impact, particularly the disproportionate effect of a 3000€ gain. There is no reference to the probability of zero outcomes or the asymmetry in the distribution of outcomes. The decision reason requires an evaluation of skewness, specifically the proportion of probability on unfavorable outcomes, and a preference for the more right-skewed lottery. Since the individual does not mention skewness or any comparison based on the distribution of probabilities across outcomes, the reason was not used. The justification is based on risk aversion and subjective value, not on skewness. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
